# Cloud pricing

The anti-seat-pricing stance, made obvious in **one table** — no calculator, no slider, nothing
else on screen. Every other tool bills per seat, so the bill explodes with team size; we show that
explosion at 10, 50 and 100 people. We don't price on people at all: you get your own nexus — a
machine that's yours, running everything you build, with the storage to match — for one flat price.
Seats never enter it, so the Workbooks row stays the same across every seat column. The stack here
is the collaborative + dev tools a team rents by the head (Notion, Linear, ClickUp, Retool,
Vercel) — Retool alone is $50/seat.

client :pricing do
  <section id="cloud-pricing">
    <div class="cp-inner">
      <p class="cp-kicker"><span class="dot"></span>the cloud · pricing</p>
      <h2 class="cp-h">Everyone bills per seat.<br>We give you a machine.</h2>
      <p class="cp-sub">Not per seat, not per user, not per anything. You get your own nexus — a machine that's yours, running everything you build — for one flat price. Put the whole team on it.</p>

      <table class="cp-table cp-compare">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th class="tool">The usual stack</th>
            <th class="num">10 seats</th>
            <th class="num">50 seats</th>
            <th class="num">100 seats</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td class="bc"><img class="g" src="brands/notion.svg" alt="" width="20" height="20"> Notion <span class="seat">$20/seat</span></td><td class="num">$200</td><td class="num">$1,000</td><td class="num">$2,000</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="bc"><img class="g" src="brands/linear.svg" alt="" width="20" height="20"> Linear <span class="seat">$16/seat</span></td><td class="num">$160</td><td class="num">$800</td><td class="num">$1,600</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="bc"><img class="g" src="brands/clickup.svg" alt="" width="20" height="20"> ClickUp <span class="seat">$12/seat</span></td><td class="num">$120</td><td class="num">$600</td><td class="num">$1,200</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="bc"><img class="g" src="brands/retool.svg" alt="" width="20" height="20"> Retool <span class="seat">$50/seat</span></td><td class="num">$500</td><td class="num">$2,500</td><td class="num">$5,000</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="bc"><img class="g" src="brands/vercel.svg" alt="" width="20" height="20"> Vercel <span class="seat">$20/seat</span></td><td class="num">$200</td><td class="num">$1,000</td><td class="num">$2,000</td></tr>
          <tr class="total"><td class="bc">The whole stack</td><td class="num">$1,180</td><td class="num">$5,900</td><td class="num">$11,800</td></tr>
